-- title:
--   Completion at n replaces G by its stabilizer
-- statement:
--   Let $O$ be a Noetherian commutative local ring with maximal ideal $\mathfrak m$, and let $C$ be a commutative $O$-algebra that is finite as an $O$-module and for which the $O$-action is faithful in the sense that $O \to C$ is injective on scalars. Let $G$ be a finite group acting on $C$ by ring automorphisms, the action commuting with that of $O$, and assume $\mathrm{Algebra.IsInvariant}\ O\ C\ G$: every $G$-fixed element of $C$ lies in the image of $O$. Let $\mathfrak n$ be a maximal ideal of $C$ lying over $\mathfrak m$, and write $D = \mathrm{MulAction.stabilizer}\ G\ \mathfrak n$, $\widehat O = \mathrm{AdicCompletion}\ \mathfrak m\ O$ and $\widehat C = \mathrm{AdicCompletion}\ \mathfrak n\ C$, the latter with the $\widehat O$-algebra structure and $D$-action provided by the scoped Galois-action instances. Then four assertions hold simultaneously: every element of $\widehat C$ fixed by $D$ lies in the image of $\widehat O$; the map $\widehat O \to \widehat C$ is injective; $\widehat C$ is a finite $\widehat O$-module; and the inertia subgroup in $D$ of the ideal of $\widehat C$ generated by the image of $\mathfrak n$ coincides with the intersection of the inertia subgroup of $\mathfrak n$ in $G$ with $D$, viewed as a subgroup of $D$.
--
--   This is the passage from a finite group acting on a semilocal extension to the decomposition group acting on the completion at a single maximal ideal upstairs, with the invariant-ring, injectivity, finiteness and inertia statements needed to recognise $\widehat O \to \widehat C$ as a Galois-type extension of complete local rings. It is used in the local study of the completions, for instance in the identification of completions at non-maximal primes as regular local rings, in domain and integral-closedness statements under tameness, and in the comparison of a completion at a point of a smooth relative curve with a power series ring.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_Algebra_IsInvariant_isInvariant_adicCompletion_stabilizer_and_injective_and_finite.lean

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_AdicCompletionGaloisAction

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

set_option autoImplicit false

open scoped Pointwise
open scoped AdicCompletion.GaloisAction

theorem Algebra.IsInvariant.isInvariant_adicCompletion_stabilizer_and_injective_and_finite
    {O : Type*} [CommRing O] [IsNoetherianRing O] [IsLocalRing O]
    {C : Type*} [CommRing C] [Algebra O C] [Module.Finite O C] [FaithfulSMul O C]
    {G : Type*} [Group G] [Finite G] [MulSemiringAction G C] [SMulCommClass G O C]
    [Algebra.IsInvariant O C G]
    (𝔫 : Ideal C) [𝔫.IsMaximal] [𝔫.LiesOver (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal O)] :
    Algebra.IsInvariant (AdicCompletion (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal O) O) (AdicCompletion 𝔫 C)
        (MulAction.stabilizer G 𝔫) ∧
    Function.Injective
        (algebraMap (AdicCompletion (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal O) O) (AdicCompletion 𝔫 C)) ∧
    Module.Finite (AdicCompletion (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal O) O) (AdicCompletion 𝔫 C) ∧
    (𝔫.map (algebraMap C (AdicCompletion 𝔫 C))).inertia (MulAction.stabilizer G 𝔫) =
        (𝔫.inertia G).subgroupOf (MulAction.stabilizer G 𝔫) := by sorry
